<title>PERU: Peru's Edegel Q3 net rises 77.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Peru's Edegel Q3 net rises 77.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Share - N.A.</p>
<p>Net - 122.46 million soles vs 69.11 million soles.</p>
<p>Revs - 282.30 million soles vs 256.76 million soles.</p>
<p>NOTES: Edegel, a Peruvian electricity generator, began trading on the Lima Stock Exchange earlier this year.</p>
<p>The Generandes consortium, consisting of Endesa de Chile, Peru's Banco Wiese and local company Grana y Montero, bought a 60 percent stake in Edegel for $524.45 when it was privatized in October 1995.</p>
<p>-- Renzo Pipoli, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
